# Portal styling: Tailwind first

Tailwind CSS is the **main styling system** for `portal/`. Prefer utility classes in components over new CSS files.

## Do

- Style new UI with Tailwind utilities (`flex`, `gap-*`, `text-muted`, `bg-surface`, `border-border`, `text-primary`, etc.).
- Use design tokens from `portal/src/styles/tokens.css` via the `@theme` map in `portal/src/styles/index.css` (e.g. `bg-primary`, `text-foreground`, `font-sans`).
- Keep shared legacy classes (`.panel`, `.btn`, `.page-shell`) only where they already exist; migrate toward Tailwind when touching those screens.
- Put any remaining non-Tailwind CSS under `portal/src/styles/` (`components/`, `pages/`, `certificates/`) and import it only from `portal/src/styles/index.css`.

## Do not

- Add new co-located page/component `.css` files next to `.tsx` files.
- Import CSS from individual pages or components (except the single entry `import "./styles/index.css"` in `main.tsx`).
- Invent parallel color systems; extend `tokens.css` + `@theme` instead.

## Certificates / print layouts

Dense print/PDF certificate markup may keep dedicated CSS under `portal/src/styles/certificates/`. Still avoid scattering imports outside `styles/index.css`.
